WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.668
-My next guest is
a very funny comedian

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.271
and a talented actor who you can
see in the new movie "Respect,"

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.973
which is in theaters
this Friday,

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.475
and his stand-up special,
"You Know What It Is,"

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.211
is on HBO Max August 19th.

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:15.748
Everyone, please welcome
Marlon Wayans.

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.950
♪ -Marlon Wayans ♪

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.053
♪ You know what it is ♪

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.821
♪ Comes from the family ♪

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.124
♪ With far too many kids ♪

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.058
♪ It's Marlon Wayans ♪

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:28.394
♪ Ain't playing no games ♪

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:32.531
♪ So when you see him,
put some respect on his name ♪

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:34.233
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:37.937
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.438
-That feels good, right?

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:40.706
-Thank you.
-That's for you.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:42.808
You look sharp.
-They think I'm Damon.

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:44.844
That's what it is.
-No, they don't.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:48.113
-I can't believe I'm second
guest to Barbra Streisand.

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:50.383
Do you understand I was hoping
she was going to be here?

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.984
-Yeah.
-Yeah, because I owe her

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:55.688
an apology 'cause I met her
one time.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.090
And I don't know
if she remembers.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.625
It was on the lot.
it was a couple years ago.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.161
She was on an NBC lot,
and I was doing "Marlon,"

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.263
and she was there,
and she was in a golf cart,

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:06.466
and she got out and I said --

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.567
everybody was like, "Barbra
Streisand, Barbra Streisand!"

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.504
And I screamed out,
"I love you, Yentl!"

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:14.240
And she took off in
that golf cart so fast.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.841
-Yentl, yeah.

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:17.577
You absolutely --
[ Laughs ]

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.812
I want to talk about
your stand-up special,

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.714
but I also want to
talk about "Respect."

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:22.782
-Yes.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.417
-Let's start with
the stand-up special.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.484
-Yes.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:27.053
-You've always --

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.421
No, you actually -- You haven't
always done stand-up.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.323
-No, I did stand-up --
I started --

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.625
See, I didn't always
do stand-up 'cause --

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.161
I come from a family
full of comedians.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.429
-Oh, yeah. Damon.
-All my brothers.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.031
Like, all of them,
they all comedians,

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.666
and I was like, "I want to do
something different,"

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:43.302
so I wanted to be
the actor of the family.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:45.204
I was like,
"You silly Negroes.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:48.074
[ English accent ] You go ahead
with your buffoonery.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.476
I'm going to be
a serious, dramatic actor."

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.344
-Yeah. "Hand me my skull."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.514
-[ Normal voice ] So I didn't
do stand-up for years.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.416
I studied drama.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:59.152
Because I felt like
when you do stand-up, right,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:03.456
you pull from your life, and I
got six comedians before me,

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.458
and we all grew up
in the same house.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.859
I ain't got [bleep]
to talk about.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.194
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.396
-They took it all.
-They got all the stories.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.597
-They took all the comedy.

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.966
-So I was like,
"I'm not gonna do stand-up."

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:18.004
And then, you know, I just was
like -- I caught the bug.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.538
I had to do a movie
for my brother called

00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:21.774
"Behind the Smile,"
and then I had to audition

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.742
for the prior movie and I was
like, "You know what?

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:24.911
I'm going to start
doing stand-up."

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.013
And I started doing stand-up
12 years ago,

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.314
and I just haven't stopped.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.249
-I'm glad you kept going.
This is great.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:31.817
-And you know what?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:33.019
Thank you.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.753
You know what made me
quit stand-up?

00:02:34.753 --> 00:02:37.357
Like, I was doing it, right,
when I was like 18, 19,

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:40.193
and then one day,
Chris Rock heckled me.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.262
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.529
-Wow.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:45.098
-And I quit stand-up
for 20 years.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.599
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.935
I was on stage and you know how
you tryin' to find it, right?

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:51.404
And I was on stage and I was
like, "Uh, so what else --

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.073
what else is up?"
He goes, "How about some jokes?"

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:57.176
And I was like --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.577
And I didn't know who it was.

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:02.581
All I kept hearing was his
evil laugh, "ha, ha, ha, ha."

00:03:02.581 --> 00:03:05.684
"How about being funny?!
How about that?!"

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:09.222
And I swear I quit stand-up
for like 20 years,

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.524
and what's funny is now I'm,
like, the baby of all --

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.326
I grew up with Eddie, Chris.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.727
All of them are
like my big brothers,

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.263
and they, like, haze me
with my older brothers.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.298
But see, I'm the baby, right,
of the bunch.

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:22.935
So now, I'm gonna pay them back
'cause they all getting old.

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.704
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.739
In about 10 years,
12 years from now,

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.474
when Chris is old and senile,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.409
and he on stage
trying to find it,

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:33.746
I'm like, "How about some jokes,
you black, skinny bastard?"

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.482
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.951
-Oh, my gosh.
[ Applause ]

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:41.153
He's gonna kill you.
-"Where the jokes?!

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:42.288
Look in your Pamper!"

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:46.458
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:48.228
-It's called
"You Know What It Is."

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:51.697
-Yes.
-It's on HBO Max August 19th.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:54.133
Congrats on that,
but let's talk about "Respect"

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.035
because this is a dramatic part.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.903
You're not funny in this.
-No, not at all.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:03:59.238
-No.
-No.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:00.840
-So I just want to set people up
for when they see this,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.341
but this is about
Aretha Franklin.

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:05.344
-Yeah, who is, you know,
like, the Queen of Soul

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:07.046
but a goddess in my household.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.981
My whole family love
Aretha Franklin.

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:10.650
Like my mama, my sisters.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.687
My sister Elvira was by --
The "Sparkle" soundtrack was on,

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.255
and she was by the radio
and she's...

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:19.358
♪ Giving him something
he could feel ♪

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:22.228
And she was 15 years old, and my
mama said, "What the hell?

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.863
You know what he wants to feel!"

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.464
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:27.266
And my sister got quiet, right?

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.535
And then six months later,

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.036
she showed up pregnant
with my nephew,

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:36.175
so she knew what
she was talking about.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.310
-Yeah, she actually did.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.147
Do you get to improvise
when you do these --

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.982
-No, you don't improvise
when you do drama.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.884
You have to be really skilled
to do that.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:48.788
Forest actually improvised
in a scene and -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.055
-Forest Whitaker?

00:04:50.055 --> 00:04:51.390
-Forest Whitaker,
who's in the movie.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.591
Fantastic actor.

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:53.826
We're in a scene,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.228
and it was the scene
where I come to the house.

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:59.565
Aretha was gonna leave C.L.
for Ted, right?

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.968
-Yeah.
-Forest plays the father.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:04.470
I play the abusive boyfriend,
her husband.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.340
So I'm about to take her
from him and he goes,

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.008
"You ain't going to do that
in my house."

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:12.111
And the man pulled out a gun.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.647
And it wasn't in the script
and you --

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.982
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:18.818
If you don't listen -- if you --

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.721
We was like, "Oh, man!
Ghost Dog went postal!

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.621
Oh, my God!"

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:25.892
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:28.494
-"Ghost Dog went postal."
-I'm serious.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:31.063
It was like, "Ah, last king of
Scotland lost his damn mind!"

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:33.900
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.235
-It is an interesting story

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.437
and a tricky story,
Aretha's story.

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:41.407
But, man, you're great in it,
and I love that you do --

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.908
These are both out
at the same time.

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:45.110
You have a comedy and a drama,
and it's tough to do.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.579
-I want to do it all, man.

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:49.281
I want to be one of those guys
that, you know, can do it all,

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:53.185
like, you know, Tom Hanks and
Robin Williams, Eddie Murphy.

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:55.621
You know, I've been studying
30 years to try

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.223
and just be my best me.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:59.792
And what do you do with a guy
that can do everything?

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.494
He does everything.
-There you go, bud.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.829
-I just love it.
-Please keep doing everything.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:05.130
Come back. We love ya.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.433
I want to show everyone a clip
from the movie.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.501
Here's Marlon Wayans
in "Respect."

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.303
Take a look at this.

00:06:11.303 --> 00:06:13.639
-What are you drinking?

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.040
-Iced tea.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.742
-Mm.

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:21.847
Just...iced tea?

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:23.816
-With a little bourbon.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.219
-[ Chuckles ]

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:28.321
Yeah, you look like
a bourbon girl.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.359
How long you in town for?
-A week.

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.261
Then I return to Tennessee.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.929
-Well, then I won't waste
any time.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.464
-Mm.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.932
-I'd like to take you out.

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.134
-Mm.

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:43.369
I'd like you to take me out.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:46.105
-How about tonight?

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:51.310
-Ree, come and help me
set this table.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.780
-Yes, to tonight.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.881
-Okay.

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:57.182
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:57.182 --> 00:06:58.918
-Marlon Wayans, everybody.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.454
"Respect" is in theaters
this Friday,

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:04.323
and his stand-up,
"You Know What It Is,"

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:07.026
is on HBO Max August 19th.

